1
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:42,000
The Switch is a crime film directed by Peter Maxwell.

2
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:18,000
A wristwatch-smuggling gang bring watches into the
country in a car's petrol tank.

3
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Poor Zena Marshall knows too much, so the gangs abducts her.

4
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Stalwart customs official Anthony Steel struggles manfully to rescue the girl.

5
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Bill Craddock, played by Anthony Steel.

6
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Caroline Markham, played by Zena Marshall.

7
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:18,000
John Curry, played by Conrad Phillips.

8
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Inspector Tomlinson, played by Dermot Walsh.

9
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:30,000
Search Officer, played by Susan Shaw.

10
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Janice Lampton, played by Dawn Beret.

11
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:42,000
The Switch is a 1963 British crime drama film directed by Peter Maxwell, and
starring Anthony Steel, Zena Marshall and Conrad Phillips.

12
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
It was written by Philip Ridgeway and Colin Fraser.

13
00:59:48,000 --> 00:59:54,000
The film concerns a criminal gang that smuggles watches into the UK
by hiding them in the petrol tank of a woman's car.

14
01:04:24,000 --> 01:04:30,000
It was Susan Shaw's last film.
